From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: with EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF a refused upload is retried without a limit unless EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES sets one (waveydude's 0924), off by default

What: 0664 (his 0919) gives an image up at its 8th refusal in a row: CpuModified is cleared and the
image is drawn with what it holds. waveydude's finding: under a long shortage that is every waiting
image, about 630 frames after the shortage began, and an image that was never uploaded is black
until the game writes it again.

Now the default is no limit: the image is tried again for as long as it is used, 128 frames apart
at most, which costs one refused attempt each time. EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES=<n> (1 or more)
brings a limit back; "0" or text that is not a number is no limit.

Off (EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF unset): nothing of 0664 runs, so nothing changes. Not in the
kept-store stamp.

Origin and credit: waveydude, patch 0924 ("Keep retrying a refused texture upload instead of
giving the image up") and headless/upload_retry.h, commit 2ca0fdb.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index c54e7d3..8082a3f 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -4646,10 +4646,13 @@ void TextureCache<P>::UploadLater(Image& image) {
     // then 128 frames (RefreshContents skips the image until then), and with
     // EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES=<n> the image is given up at its n-th refusal in a row: drawn
     // with what it holds until the guest writes it again. Off: as before (no wait, no limit).
+    // 0665 (waveydude's 0924): no limit unless EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES asks for one. An image
+    // given up for good stays black until the game writes it again, and under a long shortage
+    // that was every waiting image (~630 frames in); now it is tried every 128 frames at most.
     if (UploadBackoff()) {
         image.upload_fail_count = UploadRetry::NextFailCount(image.upload_fail_count);
         static const u32 max_retries =
-            UploadRetry::ReadMaxRetries(std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES"), 8);
+            UploadRetry::ReadMaxRetries(std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES"), 0);
         if (UploadRetry::GiveUp(image.upload_fail_count, max_retries)) {
             if (const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BAD_ALLOC_ENDS"); value && value[0] == '1') {
                 throw std::bad_alloc{};
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/upload_retry.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/upload_retry.h
index ca557b4..ab4cee0 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/upload_retry.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/upload_retry.h
@@ -23,7 +23,8 @@ constexpr std::uint64_t BackoffFrames(std::uint32_t fail_count) {
 }
 
 /// EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_MAX_RETRIES as text: the refusals in a row after which the image is given up.
-/// No text: `unset`. "0", or text that does not start with a digit: 0, never given up.
+/// No text: `unset` (0665: UploadLater passes 0, no limit, as waveydude's 0924; 0664 passed his
+/// 0919's 8). "0", or text that does not start with a digit: 0, never given up.
 inline std::uint32_t ReadMaxRetries(const char* text, std::uint32_t unset) {
     if (text == nullptr) {
         return unset;
